    "title": "Mine and yours: saying who owns it",
    "pattern": "mine / yours / his / hers / ours / theirs",
    "meaningZh": "我的／你的等，独立代替名词短语",
    "meaningEn": "Possessive pronouns without a following noun",
    "explanation": "mine、yours、hers、ours和theirs可以独立代替带所属关系的名词短语，例如mine代替my shirt。它们后面不再接名词，也不加撇号。his既可以放在名词前，也可以独立使用。先用上下文说明是哪件物品，再用这些代词指出主人。",
    "usage": "在已经明确物品的对话中说明归属，避免重复名词。",
    "nuance": "The shirt is hers说主人是谁；She is wearing the shirt说穿戴动作，两者并不必然证明同一个人拥有它。",
    "structure": [
      "my + noun → mine",
      "your + noun → yours",
      "his + noun → his; her + noun → hers",
      "our + noun → ours; their + noun → theirs"
    ],
    "formation": [
      "my + noun → mine",
      "your + noun → yours",
      "his + noun → his; her + noun → hers",
      "our + noun → ours; their + noun → theirs"
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "target": "The blue shirt is mine.",
        "zh": "蓝衬衫是我的。"
      },
      {
        "target": "Is this jacket yours?",
        "zh": "这件夹克是你的吗？"
      },
      {
        "target": "The red skirt is hers.",
        "zh": "红裙子是她的。"
      },
      {
        "target": "These shoes are ours.",
        "zh": "这些鞋是我们的。"
      }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "学习目标：在已经明确物品的对话中说明归属，避免重复名词。",
      "等级与词频为教学编排，不是官方穷尽清单或语料库测量。"
    ],
